off-board, so either the bytes arriving differ from the bytes sent, or they are
being corrupted after arrival. This board has a documented history of the
latter -- a G2D DMA overrun shredding whatever heap object sat behind the
framebuffer -- and that failure also surfaced far from its cause.

So: print what the parser actually saw. A valid chain starts 30 82 (SEQUENCE,
2-byte length). Anything else means the buffer was written over and no amount
of TLS-side fixing will help.

Also removes the clock_settime() hack while we are here -- see the comment at
the removal site for why it has to go now rather than later.
